<title>USA: Air Canada to buy Airbus planes.</title>
<headline>Air Canada to buy Airbus planes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air Canada said Friday that it signed a  letter of intent to acquire eight A330 and A340 aircraft from Airbus  Industrie, with options for 20 additional aircraft.</p>
<p>The value of the eight aircraft, based on list prices, is about $1.4  billion, a news release issued by Air Canada said.</p>
<p>Air Canada said it will become the first scheduled airline in North  America to operate the A330-300 when it takes delivery of the first  aircraft in October 1999.</p>
</text>
